--! A test platform's one capability: write the directory tree `Io.readDir`'s
--! fixtures list into the program's working directory, since a fixture
--! stages only its `.beni` files and a tree needs names, subdirectories and
--! links a source file cannot be.

--| Write `data/` below the working directory: files `b.txt`, `a.txt`,
--| `Z.txt`, `é.txt`, `ｱ.txt` (U+FF71) and `😀.txt` (U+1F600); the
--| directories `sub/` (holding `inner.txt`) and `empty/` (holding nothing
--| but `.keep`); the links `link` to `a.txt`, `dangling` to nothing and
--| `loop` to itself.
pub foreign impure makeTree : ⊤ → ⊤
